{"name":"Presidio Peach","hex":"#ec9580","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"presidio","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A garrisoned place, especially one that is or was once under Spanish control."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/presidio"},{"term":"peach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any tree of species Prunus persica, native to China and now widely cultivated throughout temperate regions, having pink flowers and edible fruit.","Soft juicy stone fruit of the peach tree, having yellow flesh, downy, red-tinted yellow skin, and a deeply sculptured pit or stone containing a single seed."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the color peach.","Particularly pleasing or agreeable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Presidio","blocks":[{"text":"A presidio was a fortified base established by the Spanish Empire mainly between the 16th and 18th centuries in areas under their control or influence. The term is derived from the Latin word praesidium meaning protection or defense."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Castillo_%288701891365%29.jpg/330px-Castillo_%288701891365%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Presidio","wikidata":"Q3323096"},{"title":"Peach","blocks":[{"text":"The peach is a deciduous tree that bears edible juicy fruits with various characteristics. Most are simply called peaches, while the glossy-skinned, non-fuzzy varieties are called nectarines. Though from the same species, they are regarded commercially as different fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg/330px-Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach","wikidata":"Q13189"},{"title":"Peach (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Peach is a color that is named for the pale color of the interior flesh of the peach fruit. Like the color apricot, the color peach is paler than most actual peach fruits and seems to have been formulated primarily to create a pastel palette of colors for interior design."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach_(color)","wikidata":"Q5148721"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Porto_Ercole_-_Vista_fortezza_dalla_rocca.JPG/250px-Porto_Ercole_-_Vista_fortezza_dalla_rocca.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Porto_Ercole_-_Vista_fortezza_dalla_rocca.JPG/500px-Porto_Ercole_-_Vista_fortezza_dalla_rocca.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Porto_Ercole_-_Vista_fortezza_dalla_rocca.JPG/250px-Porto_Ercole_-_Vista_fortezza_dalla_rocca.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APorto_Ercole_-_Vista_fortezza_dalla_rocca.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Forte_Stella_Porto_Ercole_%28GR%29.jpg/250px-Forte_Stella_Porto_Ercole_%28GR%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Forte_Stella_Porto_Ercole_%28GR%29.jpg/500px-Forte_Stella_Porto_Ercole_%28GR%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Forte_Stella_Porto_Ercole_%28GR%29.jpg/250px-Forte_Stella_Porto_Ercole_%28GR%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AForte_Stella_Porto_Ercole_(GR).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimed